---
// AI development adoption: AI coding and review with the standards that keep quality high.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageIntro from '../../components/ui/PageIntro.astro';
import Flow from '../../components/ui/Flow.astro';
import SectionHead from '../../components/ui/SectionHead.astro';
import Signals from '../../components/ui/Signals.astro';
import Related from '../../components/ui/Related.astro';
import Together from '../../components/services/Together.astro';
import Contact from '../../components/Contact.astro';
import { service } from '../../data/services';
import { url } from '../../site';

const s = service('ai-adoption');
---

<Base title={`${s.name} · craigsworks`} description={s.description} path={`services/${s.slug}/`} current="services">
  <PageIntro
    crumb={{ parent: 'services', href: '#services', here: s.name.toLowerCase() }}
    kicker={s.name.toLowerCase()}
    title={s.title}
    lede={s.lede}
    second={{ text: 'Start with a health check', href: url('services/health-check/') }}
  >
    <figure slot="side" class="tile pr">
      <div class="pr-head">
        <span class="mono">#482 · Add retry to the export job</span>
        <span class="pill pill-medium">AI risk: amber</span>
      </div>
      <div class="pr-body">
        <p class="label">ai review · against the repo's guidelines</p>
        <ul class="dash small">
          <li>Retries a non-idempotent write: check for duplicates</li>
          <li>New config value has no default for local dev</li>
          <li>Tests cover the happy path only</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="pr-human"><span class="pill pill-high">human review</span> <span class="muted small">starts with the flagged lines</span></p>
      </div>
      <figcaption class="mono">illustrative · how a pull request is rated before anyone opens the diff</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </PageIntro>

  <Signals items={s.signals} />
  <Together steps={s.steps} />

  <section id="before" class="section wrap" aria-labelledby="before-title">
    <SectionHead
      id="before"
      kicker="what i've done before"
      title="From AI-assisted to AI-first, in a year"
      sub="Over the last twelve months I've led Hive's engineering department from first introducing AI-assisted development to the point where the vast majority of code is generated by AI and reviewed by AI alongside people."
    />
    <div class="bento">
      <div class="tile c8 pop">
        <p class="label">how a change gets made now</p>
        <Flow
          label="How a change gets made now"
          steps={[
            'task',
            { text: 'AI generates the code', tone: 'acc' },
            'in-repo guidelines',
            { text: 'AI review + risk rating', tone: 'acc' },
            'human review',
            { text: 'merged', tone: 'ok' },
          ]}
        />
        <ul class="ticks points">
          <li>Standards live in the repo, so the models and the team work to the same rules</li>
          <li>Claude rates every pull request green, amber or red, so reviewers know where to look first</li>
          <li>Terraform plans get an AI summary as a GitHub check before anyone approves them</li>
          <li>Chores like cost audits, dataset restores and stacked pull requests are one command, through 20+ Claude Code skills</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="tile c4 tone-acc result pop">
        <p class="label">the result</p>
        <p class="big">Most code</p>
        <p>now AI-generated, and reviewed by AI and people before it merges</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tile c4 pop">
        <p class="label">people, not just tools</p>
        <h3>Roles and onboarding changed too</h3>
        <p class="muted small">
          I introduced an AI Engineer role and hired for it, and new starters now largely onboard themselves from
          AI-explained documentation.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="tile c4 pop">
        <p class="label">ai in the product</p>
        <h3>An agent service that earns its keep</h3>
        <p class="muted small">
          Built with Mastra on Amazon Bedrock, in its own AWS account with its own bill, and an eval suite that runs in CI.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="tile c4 pop">
        <p class="label">ai, tested like code</p>
        <h3>Checked for invented facts</h3>
        <p class="muted small">
          My portfolio's AI assistant answers only from the site, and has its own tests for the right facts, invented ones
          and prompt injection.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="honest" class="section wrap" aria-labelledby="honest-title">
    <div class="split">
      <div class="pop">
        <p class="kicker">being straight about it</p>
        <h2 id="honest-title" class="section-title">What AI won't fix on its own</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="tile tone-soft pop">
        <p class="opening">AI makes good habits faster, and bad ones faster too. That's why we start with the groundwork.</p>
        <ul class="dash">
          <li>Unclear standards become inconsistent code, at volume</li>
          <li>Thin tests let plausible-looking mistakes through</li>
          <li>Slow CI turns quick generation into a long wait for feedback</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="muted small after">If those need work first, I'll say so, and we can start there.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Related ids={s.related} />
  <Contact title={s.cta.title} body={s.cta.body} />
</Base>

<style>
  .pr {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .pr-head {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    padding: 16px 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
  }
  .pr-body {
    padding: 18px 20px;
  }
  .pr-human {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-top: 14px !important;
    padding-top: 12px;
    border-top: 1px dashed var(--line2);
  }
  figcaption {
    padding: 10px 20px;
    background: var(--acc-soft);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .points {
    margin-top: 18px;
  }
  .result {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 12px;
  }
  .result .big {
    font-size: 2.75rem;
  }
  .opening {
    margin-bottom: 14px !important;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
  }
  .after {
    margin-top: 14px !important;
  }
</style>
